  "rule": "An arm is routable for mechanical 8-K item extraction when (1) the paired bootstrap (10,000 resamples, seed 20260926) 95% lower bound of micro-F1(arm) - micro-F1(A0) is at least -0.02, (2) its JSON-valid rate is at least 0.98, and (3) every one of its batches completed. Cost is the mean billed tokens per filing: uncached input plus output, where Codex's output already includes reasoning. A candidate is recommended only when it is routable, its usage is complete, and its cost is strictly below A0's; among such candidates the cheapest wins, ties going to the lower median wall time of its ok calls, then to plan order. Otherwise the default (A0) stays. If A0's usage is incomplete, its reported cost is a lower bound: a candidate below it is still recommended, and if a ranked candidate exists but none is below it, the result is inconclusive. Cached input, reasoning and quota percentages are reported separately, and quota percentages never enter the rule.",
